{
 "_about": "One row per Skyrim twist bone: helper bones along a limb that gauntlets and sleeves are skinned to. They are not in MORDHAU's clip; the plugin sets each from the roll of the bones around it so the mesh is not wrung. owner: bone_map row id the twist bone sits on. toward: bone_map row id the owner points at (gives the limb's axis). mode follow_child: take a share of the roll of `toward` relative to the owner (forearm twists follow the hand). mode counter_parent: undo a share of the owner's roll relative to `relative_to` (upper-arm twists stay with the shoulder). The share is the twist bone's position along the limb, read from Skyrim's rest pose.",
